.TH TRUSTD 8 "September 2026" "Peios" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
trustd \- compose and serve the Peios machine trust store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trustd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trustd
combines the packaged CA bundle with additions and distrust decisions under
.BR Machine\eSystem\eTrust .
It serves the effective set on a local socket and, when enabled, renders the
Linux-compatible certificate bundle and hashed certificate directory.
.PP
The daemon watches the registry and periodically checks the packaged bundle.
Each change recomposes the complete store. Invalid local certificates are
skipped without discarding the remaining valid trust set. If the packaged
bundle becomes unreadable, the last rendered store is retained and the daemon
reports degraded health.
.PP
After each recomposition after the first, the daemon writes one
.BR trustd.root.added ,
.B trustd.root.removed
or
.B trustd.root.distrusted
event for every root that entered or left the effective set, described in
.IR /usr/share/evman/trustd.evman .
.PP
The service runs as LocalService with its own service SID. A SYSTEM pre-start
hook creates
.I /system/retc/ssl
and grants that service SID access; the daemon itself does not need elevated
privilege and holds no private key. Its service SID is granted
.B SeAuditPrivilege
alone, to write those events.
.SH RELOADING
SIGHUP asks the running daemon to recompose its store using the same refresh
path as
.BR "trust reload" .
This supports peinit's default service reload without replacing the main
process. Repeated pending signals may be coalesced into one refresh.
If recomposition fails, the daemon retains its last rendered store and
reports degraded health. Inspect
.B trust status
for the resulting health; service reload completion alone does not prove it.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The registry schema and live settings are documented by
.IR /usr/share/regman/trustd.regman .
In particular,
.B GenerateLinuxTrustFiles
controls whether compatibility files are rendered, while
.B ControlSecurity
sets the control socket's security descriptor.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/ca-certificates/mozilla.crt
Packaged CA root bundle.
.TP
.I /run/trustd/trust.sock
Native query and control socket.
.TP
.I /system/retc/ssl
Rendered compatibility store.
.TP
.I /system/retc/prepare-store.log
Output from the privileged directory preparation hook.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trust (1),
.BR reg (1)

.SH REPLY DEADLINE
A control reply has one five-second write deadline, shared by all root-list
chunks. If the peer stops reading, the connection is closed when this budget
expires. A client must reject an incomplete snapshot.
